{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105246","id":2451636646,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6SIQGm","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105246","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105246.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105246.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105246","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105246/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105246/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105246/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ef581994ab52ed1bf45b5982afefae65fc0177b3","number":105246,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"De-duplicate a lot of `variant_internal.h`","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`variant_internal.h` (and similar headers) are currently a big old mess of duplicated logic.\r\n\r\nThis PR is a first step towards de-duplication.\r\nAs a codestyle PR, it should not affect performance (and probably won't have noticeable impact on compile time either).\r\n\r\n## Explanation\r\n\r\nIn practice, I see the following types / use-cases:\r\n- `VariantGetInternalPtr`: For types that are stored in `Variant`, get a pointer to their value.\r\n    - Some are stored behind additional logic, e.g. pooling or reference counts, indicated by `is_local`.\r\n- `VariantImplicitConvert` (new): For types that are not stored directly in `Variant`, but act as if they are, using another type as storage surrogate (e.g. `float` or enums).\r\n- `VariantInternalAccessor`: Offers an API to get or set any type that can be stored in `Variant` (both direct types and implicit conversion types).\r\n\r\nUsing this logic, structs can be simplified:\r\n- `VariantGetInternalPtr` has only 3 logical implementations (ignoring `Object`): Those that are stored in the `Variant`, those that use a pointer to a heap value, and those that use `PackedArrayRef`. This can be abstracted and de-duplicated.\r\n- `VariantInitializer` and `VariantDefaultInitializer ` for `is_local` types can just assign to the payload.\r\n- `VariantInternalAccessor` for stored types can access the stored type by reference, and for conversion types can return and accept copies.\r\n\r\n## Other changes\r\n\r\nTighter requirements on the declared types allowed me to spot a few accessor mistakes in the codebase, which I addressed.\r\n\r\n## Addendum\r\n\r\nIn follow up PRs, more duplicated logic should be removed from these headers, and duplicated functions and structs should be phased out. This is merely a first step establishing a way forward.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":27909699